\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  1.   \cf0  Just one day in heav'n abiding,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Gives more joy than thousands here.
\par Better than on earth residing
\par Which holds only grief and fear.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par If a thousand years of living
\par I would spend in vain pursuits,
\par When compared with godly virtues,
\par They would be false substitutes.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-360\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par      2.    Here is sighing, here are sorrows,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Discontent a thousand fold;
\par Where no human heart is happy,
\par Who the fear of death must hold.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par But in God's realm is no crying,
\par Neither sorrow, grief ,nor sigh.
\par Death is bound, it cannot harm them,
\par Dwelling with the Lord on high.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  There will joy continue ever
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 in that city of our Lord,
\par where the sun will shine in glory
\par and the Lamb of God adored.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par But today we lack perception
\par To define eternal things,
\par Nor can man define God's greatness
\par That His revelation brings.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  To behold the Lord and serve Him
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 My delight shall always be
\par For the same God now abiding
\par Will be ours eternally!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Lord, my longing beigniting
\par That my soul is drawn to Thee,
\par That for Thee my earnest longing;
\par \pard       Yes, forever Thine to be! \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

